  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ending Violence Against Women in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to develop and improve judicial training apparatus, champion impartiality of judges, magistrates &amp; kadhis and promote gender justice reform, diversity &amp; inclusivity. While leveraging on technology through mobile applications, the project will be providing, real time connection between survivors and GBV service, enabling survivors to get a quick and direct response with the GBV service provider and allow them to report and have a one -on -one conversation. The apps will aim to educate the masses on Gender Based Violence and also reach out to those who could be potential first responders. They will also collect data on GBV, which will help in researching and implementation of policies against GBV, which, in the long run, will create a safer environment. The apps will contribute to the de - stigmatize   mental health, reduce suicide rates and offer online therapy.</narrative>
  </description>
